ications and we've already started  doing this internally so just to clarify  once you've been authorized to access a  notebook we get out of your way you just  have to keep our platform page open in  the background to maintain that  authorized rotating connection and then  you can open the notebook itself in a  new tab full screen open a terminal  inside of it and otherwise just interact  with it like you would local notebook so  the next component in our architecture  is kubernetes so you can think that we  have all of these houses that each  contain a notebook and then we have a  front door that protects access to those  houses and now we need to put all of  these houses somewhere and that's where  kubernetes does it organizes all of  these houses so it's kind of like the  suburbs so kubernetes is an open source  system for running and managing  containerized applications we use  kubernetes to run users notebooks and  kubernetes has some great abstractions  called pods and services for deploying  multiple containers so using pods and  services we can have the notebook and  the front-door deployed together and we  can specify that the notebook is not  accessible to the rest of the world and  it's only accessible through the front  door and there are two things about  kubernetes that really stood out for us  as we used it first it just works  if you've ever if you've ever tried to  learn about kubernetes you'll know that  it's very very complicated and there's a  lot of parts to it but amazingly once  you learn how to do things it all just  works we basically had no problems with  any of the core functionality it also  has a pluggable architecture and a  decent ecosystem of plugins there were a  few plugins that we need  in order to implement this system there  was just no way to make it work without  them and while they're not as easy to  use of the core components at least they  exist and we were able to make them do  what we want now the bad about  kubernetes is